# Build-context exclusions shared by every Dockerfile in this repo.
#
# The product image is built with `COPY backend /app` from the repo root, so
# whatever sits in the working tree at build time lands in an image layer. On a
# CI runner that tree is a clean checkout, but the README documents a local
# `docker compose -f docker-compose.product.yml up --build` and instructs
# developers to create `backend/.env` — without this file that env file, the
# dev SQLite database and the local virtualenv would all be baked into a
# distributable image. Exclusions here are the boundary that makes a locally
# built image safe to hand to someone else.
#
# Note: backend/tests is deliberately NOT excluded — docker/Dockerfile.tests
# runs the backend and module-owned suites for docker-compose.test.yml.
# Stripping tests from the *product* image is a Dockerfile-side change.

.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude

# Secrets and local state — never in a build context.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
backend/dev.db

# Virtualenvs and dependency trees (reinstalled inside the image).
**/.venv
**/node_modules

# Build outputs and caches.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.coverage
htmlcov/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.vite
frontend/dist

# Not needed by any image.
docs
launcher
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
